<title>USA: PacifiCorp sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</title>
<headline>PacifiCorp sells $300 mln in 2-part deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt issue from PacifiCorp was priced Wednesday, according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>PacifiCorp is an electric services provider; coal, gas producer.</p>
<p>BORROWER PACIFICORP</p>
<p>AMT $175 MLN	 COUPON 6.75 PCT   MATURITY 7/15/2004</p>
<p>TYPE 1ST MTG BONDS ISS PRICE 99.714  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 6.802 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD +58 BPS</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 7/15/2009</p>
<p>TYPE 1ST MTG BONDS ISS PRICE 99.639  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.045 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD +80 BPS</p>
<p>NOTES: Both tranches have a make-whole-call provision at +10 basis points over the U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
